## Acceptance Notes

- Control UI first path is Telegram-style chat: conversation rail, message thread, right-side evidence/approval panel, and bottom composer.
- Control UI runtime rail remains focused on Local review / Safety / Evidence, with diagnostics collapsed.
- Native deterministic fixture keeps desktop and mobile first-read paths guarded.
- Native room status toggles require confirmation before Matrix unread/favorite/low-priority requests are sent.
- Native message edits require confirmation before the Matrix EditMessage request is sent.
- Native direct-message creation requires a second confirmation before the Matrix OpenOrCreateDirectMessage allow_create=true request is sent.
- Native selected-row route variants are covered by the fixture visual manifest.
- Native true-window route variants are covered when `HEPTA_UI_PRODUCT_READINESS_INCLUDE_NATIVE_WINDOW_ROUTE_SMOKE=1`.
- Native true-window secondary mobile surfaces are covered when `HEPTA_UI_PRODUCT_READINESS_INCLUDE_NATIVE_WINDOW_SECONDARY_MOBILE_SMOKE=1`.
- Native packaging metadata, local unsigned app bundle probe, GA readiness, and merge-completion reports are synchronized against the current worktree's local loopback server.
- Native distribution preflight checks the signing/notarization/stapling workflow statically and records release approval, credential, notary submission, and public artifact blockers without reading Apple credential values.
- True Makepad window smoke is available as an explicit opt-in gate and writes its own report, log, and desktop/mobile screenshots into this artifact.

## Local Dependency

- Combined readiness stays deterministic by default and does not require a visible unlocked desktop.
- The opt-in true Makepad window smoke requires an unlocked macOS desktop and Peekaboo Screen Recording/Accessibility permission.
- On this machine those permissions are granted; use the opt-in environment flag above to collect true window screenshots inside the combined artifact.
REPORT
